# Chaos: the helper's Auto Target only picks monsters it can reach, and takes loot goblins, bosses and special monsters
# first (after 0001-0116; numbered 0117 because other branches use 0110, 0111 and 0114). Owner request 2026-10-23: "make
# the auto target only attack reachable monsters; by default the nearest and the one with the lowest health; priority for
# loot goblins, bosses and special monsters". Before: mode F (the default) took the nearest by straight distance in the
# 7 x 5 reach window, even behind a wall or across water, and kept the lock on it. Now check() asks ChaosAutoTargetEngine
# (overlay game_autotarget, rules in ChaosAutoTarget, tested) at four points: the lock is dropped when the monster cannot be
# reached or a better class appears; the monster list is cut to the reachable ones (g_map.findPath for melee, a clear line
# of sight for the ranged classes); the pick goes to the best priority class (not in mode J, the player's own list) and
# mode F orders by the way to walk, then the lowest health. Two boxes under Always Chase Opponent, "Priority targets" and
# "Only reachable" (both on by default, g_settings chaosAutoTargetPriority / chaosAutoTargetReachable), switch the rules off;
# the panel grows by two 22px rows. Without the module the base behaviour stays.
